WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:03.170
In Hollywood, there are more actors than parts.

00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:06.670
When you're trying to get a career going,
rejection is par for the course.

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:10.710
Still, it's hard to believe some of these
failed auditions that cost huge actors some

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:11.890
legendary roles…

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:13.820
Robert De Niro - The Godfather

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:18.640
Sure, he won Best Supporting Actor for playing
young Vito Corleone in The Godfather Part

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:19.640
II.

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:23.019
But Robert De Niro actually auditioned for
the part of Sonny in the first Godfather movie.

00:00:23.019 --> 00:00:24.080
"You gonna take both of them?

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:25.119
Nanana you gonna take them?

00:00:25.119 --> 00:00:26.989
Ey you know what they gonna do to you?

00:00:26.989 --> 00:00:29.759
Ey you know what you do when you knock somebody
off?

00:00:29.759 --> 00:00:33.530
You take a gun you shoot him right up against
his f---ing head that's what you do.

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:36.480
You get his, ya get his brains all over your
nice new Ivy League suit, Michael that's what

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:37.890
happens."

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:39.719
James Caan got it, but that's okay.

00:00:39.719 --> 00:00:40.719
Sonny was a chump.

00:00:40.719 --> 00:00:42.640
Vito was a legend.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:45.390
Seth Rogen and Bob Odenkirk - The Office

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:50.070
Between Freaks and Geeks' cancellation in
2000 and The 40-Year-Old Virgin in 2005, Seth

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:52.019
Rogen had a bit of a dry spell.

00:00:52.019 --> 00:00:55.050
During that period, he auditioned for the
role of Dwight on The Office.

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:56.670
"Urine is sterile.

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:59.170
Did you know that?

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:02.449
If you're in the field, you can clean a man's
wound by taking a whiz on it."

00:01:02.449 --> 00:01:06.680
Rainn Wilson got the part...and Rogen went
on to become an A-list actor and writer.

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:10.500
Meanwhile, Bob Odenkirk was already a comedy
legend when he auditioned for the lead role

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:11.820
of Michael Scott.

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:14.770
"We play hard, and we work hard.

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:18.910
Sometimes we uh probably play hard when we
should be working hard but that's probably

00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:24.500
my fault but...fire me."

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:28.400
He lost to Steve Carell, best known at the
time as a correspondent on The Daily Show.

00:01:28.409 --> 00:01:32.000
Odenkirk must've been pretty close, because
he guest-starred in the final season as an

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.939
eerily Michael Scott-esque boss at an office
where Pam lands an interview.

00:01:35.939 --> 00:01:36.939
"Hey guys!

00:01:36.939 --> 00:01:37.939
Say something!"

00:01:37.939 --> 00:01:38.939
"Hello!"

00:01:38.939 --> 00:01:40.399
"Hi I'm Mark!

00:01:40.399 --> 00:01:47.189
I'm the uh horrible boss around here but please
don't hire Jaimie Foxx to kill me."

00:01:47.189 --> 00:01:48.789
"Djangooooo!"

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:55.520
"I don't agree with the use of the N word
in that movie, it's too soon."

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:57.820
Scarlett Johansson - Jumanji

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:02.320
This future Avenger started as a child star—her
first big-screen role came when she was just

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:04.560
nine, in the 1994 comedy North.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:07.810
The following year, ScarJo missed out on Jumanji
to Kirsten Dunst.

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:13.099
"Would forget about the stupid game, now close
it up and put it away!"

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:15.530
Josh Hutcherson - Amazing Spider-Man

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:21.310
Every young actor between 18 and 30 probably
had a shot at Peter Parker and his agile alter-ego.

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:25.819
Josh Hutcherson had just filmed his first
Hunger Games when he showed up for this audition.

00:02:25.819 --> 00:02:27.500
One franchise would have to do.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:31.790
Despite Hutcherson's solid screen test for
2012's Amazing Spider-Man, Andrew Garfield

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:33.560
wore the webs.

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:35.860
Gwyneth Paltrow - Jurassic Park

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:38.860
Steven Spielberg cast Paltrow in a bit part
in Hook.

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:42.340
Two years later he got her an audition for
his surefire dinosaur blockbuster.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:47.420
"Or maybe, maybe it's just ritual behavior,
species specific behavior that serves to identify

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:49.240
them to one another.

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:52.890
But maybe it doesn't have any broader meaning."

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:57.170
But the future Oscar winner apparently just
wasn't as good as Laura Dern.

00:02:57.170 --> 00:02:58.240
Brad Pitt - "Backdraft"

00:02:58.240 --> 00:02:59.240
Handsome?

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:00.240
Check.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:01.240
Talented?

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:02.240
Check.

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:06.060
But in 1991, casting directors hadn't seen
Brad Pitt's full potential yet.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:07.310
He auditioned for Backdraft…

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:13.410
"Ya know, these new stations, are part of
how Commissioner Swayzak's wrecking this department."

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:17.340
But instead they went with the Brad Pitt of
1991, Billy Baldwin.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:19.879
Jeremy Sisto - Titanic

00:03:19.879 --> 00:03:24.489
Jeremy Sisto was hot off his appearance as
Elton in Clueless when he auditioned for Titanic.

00:03:24.489 --> 00:03:28.439
Today it's impossible to imagine anyone but
Leonardo DiCaprio yelling about being king

00:03:28.439 --> 00:03:32.360
of the world in the James Cameron blockbuster,
but it's still fascinating to watch his screen

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:33.709
test with Kate Winslet.

00:03:33.709 --> 00:03:34.769
"Thank you"

00:03:34.769 --> 00:03:36.370
"Oh thank you.

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:41.159
I mean, I mean thank you for thanking me.

00:03:41.159 --> 00:03:43.290
I mean you're welcome."

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:47.500
A few years after whiffing on this role, Sisto
landed a gig on Six Feet Under and went on

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:51.019
to star in Law &amp; Order, Suburgatory, and plenty
more.

00:03:51.019 --> 00:03:52.989
Kurt Russell - Star Wars

00:03:52.989 --> 00:03:56.970
Unfortunately for Kurt Russell, he auditioned
for the soon-to-be-iconic role of Han Solo

00:03:56.970 --> 00:04:01.290
against Harrison Ford, the only actor of the
era who was more effortlessly cool than Kurt

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:02.290
Russell.

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:04.390
"I was only paid to bring ya here and now
you're here.

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:07.400
So I'll just take my other 5000 and you're
on your own."

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:08.400
It's okay.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:11.019
Harrison Ford never could have handled Snake
Plissken or Jack Burton.

00:04:11.019 --> 00:04:15.540
"Ah ya know what ol Jack Burton always says
at a time like this?"

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:16.540
"Who?"

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:18.450
"Jack Burton, me!"

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:20.820
Tom Selleck - Raiders of the Lost Ark

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:24.690
It's the most famous Hollywood "what if":
Tom Selleck was offered the role of Indiana

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:29.420
Jones, but had to refuse because he was stuck
filming Magnum, P.I. Harrison Ford strikes

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:30.700
again.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:31.480
"Hello Marion."

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:39.940
"Look, I did what I did I don't expect you
to be happy about it, but maybe it can do

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:40.940
us both some good."

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:42.970
"Why start now?!"

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:45.220
"Just shut up, shut up and listen to me.

00:04:45.230 --> 00:04:47.380
Now I need that piece your father had."

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:49.040
But oh, what could've been!

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:51.880
Indiana Jones would've had a killer mustache,
for example.

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:52.880
Thanks for watching!

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:56.060
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:59.820
And leave us a comment to let us know which
actor you would've rather seen get the part...

